.TH "LOGJETD" "1" "March 2026" "" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
logjetd - OTLP ingest, \f[C].logjet\f[R] storage, replay, and file
blasting daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[C]logjetd\f[R] [\f[C]serve\f[R]] [\f[C]-c\f[R]|\f[C]--config\f[R]
\f[I]path\f[R]]
.PP
\f[C]logjetd\f[R] \f[C]inspect\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]
.PP
\f[C]logjetd\f[R] \f[C]segments\f[R] \f[C]--path\f[R] \f[I]dir\f[R]
\f[C]--name\f[R] \f[I]base.logjet\f[R]
.PP
\f[C]logjetd\f[R] \f[C]replay\f[R] [\f[C]-c\f[R]|\f[C]--config\f[R]
\f[I]path\f[R]] \f[C]--path\f[R] \f[I]dir\f[R] \f[C]--name\f[R]
\f[I]base.logjet\f[R] \f[C]--dest\f[R] \f[I]url-or-host:port\f[R]
.PP
\f[C]logjetd\f[R] \f[C]prune\f[R] \f[C]--path\f[R] \f[I]dir\f[R]
\f[C]--name\f[R] \f[I]base.logjet\f[R] [\f[C]--keep-files\f[R]
\f[I]n\f[R] | \f[C]--keep-bytes\f[R] \f[I]bytes\f[R]]
\f[C]--dry-run\f[R]
.PP
\f[C]logjetd\f[R] \f[C]bridge\f[R] [\f[C]-c\f[R]|\f[C]--config\f[R]
\f[I]path\f[R]] \f[C]--source\f[R] \f[I]host:port\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[C]logjetd\f[R] is a small telemetry daemon for constrained systems.
.PP
It can:
.IP \[bu] 2
accept OTLP/HTTP log batches on \f[C]POST /v1/logs\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
accept OTLP/gRPC log batches on the standard
\f[C]LogsService/Export\f[R] endpoint
.IP \[bu] 2
optionally run OTLP/HTTP ingest over HTTPS and OTLP/gRPC ingest over TLS
.IP \[bu] 2
store raw OTLP protobuf payloads either in memory or in append-only
\f[C].logjet\f[R] files
.IP \[bu] 2
expose a replay listener for downstream consumers over the current
internal wire protocol
.IP \[bu] 2
connect to another \f[C]logjetd\f[R] replay listener and forward backlog
plus live records into an OTLP/HTTP collector
.IP \[bu] 2
optionally protect replay and bridge transport with TLS
.IP \[bu] 2
optionally export to an HTTPS OTLP collector
.IP \[bu] 2
inspect \f[C].logjet\f[R] files and directories
.IP \[bu] 2
list file-segment metadata for one rotated spool
.IP \[bu] 2
replay stored \f[C].logjet\f[R] files into an OTLP/HTTP collector as a
one-shot operation
.IP \[bu] 2
prune oldest rotated file segments by file count or byte budget
.PP
The daemon is designed for cheap hardware, limited RAM, unreliable
storage, and intermittent downstream connectivity.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS serve
.PP
Run the daemon using configuration loaded from
\f[C]/etc/logjet.conf\f[R] by default, or from the file passed with
\f[C]-c\f[R] or \f[C]--config\f[R].
.PP
If no explicit command is given, \f[C]serve\f[R] is the default.
.PP
Current serve behaviour:
.IP \[bu] 2
OTLP/HTTP ingest is supported with \f[C]ingest.protocol: otlp-http\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
OTLP/gRPC ingest is supported with \f[C]ingest.protocol: otlp-grpc\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
a replay listener socket is exposed for downstream clients
.IP \[bu] 2
replay listener traffic currently uses the internal framed protocol, not
OTLP egress
.SS bridge
.PP
Connect to another \f[C]logjetd\f[R] replay listener, drain retained
backlog, stay attached for live records, and forward OTLP log payloads
to the configured collector.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
logjetd --config ./logjetd.conf bridge --source 10.0.0.15:7002
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
If \f[C]--source\f[R] is omitted, bridge uses \f[C]upstream.replay\f[R]
from configuration.
.SS inspect
.PP
Inspect a \f[C].logjet\f[R] file or a directory containing
\f[C].logjet\f[R] files.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
logjetd inspect /var/lib/logjet
\f[R]
.fi
.SS segments
.PP
List ordered rotated segments for one spool.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
logjetd segments --path /var/lib/logjet --name bofh.logjet
\f[R]
.fi
.SS replay
.PP
Read ordered \f[C].logjet\f[R] files from a directory and blast the
stored OTLP log payloads into an OTLP/HTTP collector.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
logjetd replay --path /var/logs --name bofh.logjet --dest http://127.0.0.1:4318/v1/logs
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Replay order is:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]bofh.logjet\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]bofh-1.logjet\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]bofh-2.logjet\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
and so on
.PP
Replay is immediate and does not preserve original timing.
If \f[C]--dest\f[R] is omitted, replay uses \f[C]collector.url\f[R] from
configuration.
.SS prune
.PP
Remove oldest rotated file segments deliberately.
.PP
Examples:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
logjetd prune --path /var/lib/logjet --name bofh.logjet --keep-files 2
logjetd prune --path /var/lib/logjet --name bofh.logjet --keep-bytes 1048576 --dry-run
\f[R]
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.SS \f[C]-c\f[R], \f[C]--config\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]
.PP
Load configuration from \f[I]path\f[R] instead of
\f[C]/etc/logjet.conf\f[R].
.SS \f[C]-h\f[R], \f[C]--help\f[R]
.PP
Print usage information.
.SS \f[C]--path\f[R] \f[I]dir\f[R]
.PP
Directory containing \f[C].logjet\f[R] files for replay.
.PP
Used with the \f[C]segments\f[R], \f[C]replay\f[R], and \f[C]prune\f[R]
commands.
.SS \f[C]--name\f[R] \f[I]base.logjet\f[R]
.PP
Base file name used to locate replay segments.
.PP
Example:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]bofh.logjet\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]bofh-1.logjet\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]bofh-2.logjet\f[R]
.PP
Used only with the \f[C]replay\f[R] command.
.SS \f[C]--keep-files\f[R] \f[I]n\f[R]
.PP
Keep only the newest \f[I]n\f[R] segment files during \f[C]prune\f[R].
.SS \f[C]--keep-bytes\f[R] \f[I]bytes\f[R]
.PP
Keep only the newest segment set that fits within \f[I]bytes\f[R] during
\f[C]prune\f[R].
.SS \f[C]--dry-run\f[R]
.PP
Show which files \f[C]prune\f[R] would remove without deleting them.
.SS \f[C]--dest\f[R] \f[I]url-or-host:port\f[R]
.PP
Destination OTLP/HTTP collector for replay.
.PP
Used only with the \f[C]replay\f[R] command.
.PP
If a full \f[C]http://host:port/path\f[R] URL is given, replay uses that
exact path.
If only \f[C]host:port\f[R] is given, replay defaults to
\f[C]/v1/logs\f[R].
.SS \f[C]--source\f[R] \f[I]host:port\f[R]
.PP
Upstream \f[C]logjetd\f[R] replay listener for the \f[C]bridge\f[R]
command.
.PP
If omitted, \f[C]bridge\f[R] uses \f[C]upstream.replay\f[R] from
configuration.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Default configuration path:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
/etc/logjet.conf
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Important keys:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
output: buffer
buffer.size: 100
buffer.messages: 5000
buffer.keep: 1500
file.path: /var/lib/logjet
file.size: 10240
file.name: vehicle.logjet
collector.url: http://127.0.0.1:4318/v1/logs
collector.timeout-ms: 10000
collector.ca-file: /etc/logjet/collector-ca.pem
collector.cert-file: /etc/logjet/collector.pem
collector.key-file: /etc/logjet/collector.key
collector.server-name: collector.internal
backpressure.enabled: false
backpressure.mode: disconnect
backpressure.max-buffered-records: 16
upstream.replay: 10.0.0.15:7002
upstream.mode: keep
upstream.state-file: /var/lib/logjet/bridge.state
upstream.retry-ms: 1000
upstream.connect-timeout-ms: 5000
tls.enable: false
tls.ca-file: /etc/logjet/ca.pem
tls.cert-file: /etc/logjet/node.pem
tls.key-file: /etc/logjet/node.key
tls.require-client-cert: false
tls.server-name: appliance.internal
ingest.protocol: otlp-http
ingest.listen: 127.0.0.1:4318
ingest.tls-enable: false
ingest.ca-file: /etc/logjet/ingest-ca.pem
ingest.cert-file: /etc/logjet/ingest.pem
ingest.key-file: /etc/logjet/ingest.key
ingest.require-client-cert: false
ingest.max-batch-bytes: 1048576
ingest.max-clients: 32
ingest.max-batches-per-second: 0
ingest.priority-severity-at-least: error
ingest.overload-report-ms: 5000
replay.listen: 0.0.0.0:7002
replay.max-clients: 32
replay.client-timeout-ms: 10000
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Rules:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]buffer.size\f[R] is measured in KiB
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]file.size\f[R] is measured in KiB
.IP \[bu] 2
set either \f[C]buffer.size\f[R] or \f[C]buffer.messages\f[R], never
both
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]buffer.keep\f[R] applies only to memory mode
.IP \[bu] 2
file mode always keeps all rotated files
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]segments\f[R] and \f[C]prune\f[R] provide explicit operator tooling
for file-mode archive housekeeping
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]ingest.protocol\f[R] supports \f[C]wire\f[R], \f[C]otlp-http\f[R],
and \f[C]otlp-grpc\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]ingest.max-batch-bytes\f[R] rejects oversized OTLP or wire payloads
before they are stored
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]ingest.max-clients\f[R] caps concurrent ingest handling
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]ingest.max-batches-per-second\f[R] caps accepted ingest batches per
second
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]ingest.priority-severity-at-least\f[R] lets higher-severity OTLP
log batches bypass overload shedding
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]ingest.overload-report-ms\f[R] controls operator-visible overload
summaries on stderr
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]replay.max-clients\f[R] caps concurrent replay clients
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]replay.client-timeout-ms\f[R] caps how long one replay client can
block on socket I/O
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]collector.url\f[R] configures replay destination URL
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]collector.timeout-ms\f[R] configures replay and bridge socket
timeout in milliseconds
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]collector.ca-file\f[R], \f[C]collector.cert-file\f[R],
\f[C]collector.key-file\f[R], and \f[C]collector.server-name\f[R]
configure HTTPS collector export
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]backpressure.enabled\f[R] enables bridge backpressure policy
handling
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]backpressure.mode\f[R] configures whether bridge export blocks,
disconnects, or drops newest records when the collector is too slow
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]backpressure.max-buffered-records\f[R] caps the bridge-side
exporter queue per bridge connection
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]upstream.replay\f[R] configures the default bridge source
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]upstream.mode\f[R] configures whether bridge keeps or drains
upstream retained records
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]upstream.state-file\f[R] stores persisted bridge resume state
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]upstream.retry-ms\f[R] configures bridge reconnect delay
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]upstream.connect-timeout-ms\f[R] configures bridge source connect
timeout
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]ingest.*\f[R] configures optional TLS on OTLP/HTTP and OTLP/gRPC
ingest
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]tls.*\f[R] configures optional TLS for replay listener and bridge
transport
.SH STORAGE MODES
.SS Buffer mode
.PP
In-memory ring behaviour:
.IP \[bu] 2
first \f[C]buffer.keep\f[R] messages are retained in a permanent front
jar
.IP \[bu] 2
later messages form a rotating FIFO tail
.PP
Drain model:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
[kept messages][rotating tail]
\f[R]
.fi
.SS File mode
.PP
Append-only file behaviour:
.IP \[bu] 2
write to \f[C]name.logjet\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
rotate to \f[C]name-1.logjet\f[R], \f[C]name-2.logjet\f[R], and so on
when \f[C]file.size\f[R] is exceeded
.IP \[bu] 2
old rotated files are kept
.SH CURRENT FEATURES
.IP \[bu] 2
OTLP/HTTP log ingest on \f[C]POST /v1/logs\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
OTLP/gRPC log ingest on the standard logs export service
.IP \[bu] 2
optional TLS on OTLP/HTTP and OTLP/gRPC ingest
.IP \[bu] 2
basic ingest guardrails through \f[C]ingest.max-batch-bytes\f[R] and
\f[C]ingest.max-clients\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
ingest rate limiting with severity-aware overload shedding
.IP \[bu] 2
append-only \f[C].logjet\f[R] file output with size-based rotation
.IP \[bu] 2
in-memory ring buffering with \f[C]buffer.keep\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
replay listener for downstream consumers using the internal framed
protocol
.IP \[bu] 2
independent replay cursor per connected client
.IP \[bu] 2
basic replay-client caps through \f[C]replay.max-clients\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
basic replay-client timeout through \f[C]replay.client-timeout-ms\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
continuous bridge mode from replay listener to OTLP/HTTP collectors
.IP \[bu] 2
acknowledged drain mode through \f[C]upstream.mode: drain\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
persisted bridge resume through \f[C]upstream.state-file\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
upstream restart and storage-replacement detection through replay stream
identity
.IP \[bu] 2
basic backpressure policy through \f[C]backpressure.mode\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
bounded bridge-side exporter queue through
\f[C]backpressure.max-buffered-records\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
optional TLS on replay/bridge transport
.IP \[bu] 2
HTTPS OTLP collector export
.IP \[bu] 2
one-shot file replay to OTLP/HTTP collectors with
\f[C]logjetd replay\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
configurable replay destination via \f[C]collector.url\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
inspection of \f[C].logjet\f[R] files and directories
.SH CURRENT LIMITATIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
replay listener traffic is not OTLP
.IP \[bu] 2
upstream storage reset and rollover handling is still basic
.IP \[bu] 2
ingest overload handling is limited to payload-size caps and
concurrent-client caps
.IP \[bu] 2
multi-client replay isolation is still basic beyond per-client cursors
and replay-client caps
.IP \[bu] 2
file mode does not delete old rotated files
.IP \[bu] 2
certificate management and deployment policy are still operator-managed
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run the daemon with explicit config:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
logjetd --config ./logjetd.conf
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Inspect generated files:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
logjetd inspect ./logs
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Replay files to a local collector:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
logjetd --config ./logjetd.conf replay --path ./logs --name bofh.logjet
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Bridge from a remote replay listener into a collector:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
logjetd --config ./logjetd.conf bridge --source 10.0.0.15:7002
\f[R]
.fi
